# /model while a turn is still streaming: it is a UI-only command (like
# /mcp), so it opens its dialog right away instead of waiting for the
# busy turn to end. The in-flight reply keeps streaming from the model
# that was current when it started; the switch only takes effect for the
# NEXT turn.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/dialogs-model-switch-mid-stream.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE start the slow turn
KEY enter
WAITFOR /working on it/ 10
SHOT turn-streaming
TYPE /model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Select model/ 10
SHOT dialog-open-while-busy
EXPECT /Select model/
KEY down
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Now on faux\/faux-2 · small tier/ 10
SHOT switched-while-still-streaming
WAITFOR /Finished the slow turn\./ 20
SHOT first-turn-completed-on-old-model
EXPECT /Finished the slow turn\./
TYPE second turn on the new model
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Second turn on faux-2\./ 20
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
